Good thread. My honest rule of thumb: before adding any dependency, I ask whether I could write the needed piece in under a day, and whether the package is maintained, widely used, and has a clear license. I learned this the hard way after pulling in a tiny parsing library that went unmaintained and later needed a patch I couldn't land upstream.

@delta_panda34, I'd check `fastjson-utils2`'s maintenance history, release cadence, and who owns it before relying on it. Small packages carry supply-chain risk, and a benchmark on your own data beats a claimed speedup.

Also, before shipping, do a quick threat model of each new dependency: what it can access, and what happens if it's compromised.

