For me it's the boring stuff: a tiny cron-driven cost and runtime report. Every morning it dumps a one-page table of spend per tag, longest-running job, and any job that's been idle for more than a few hours.

Three metrics cover most of it: daily spend vs. budget, jobs running past their expected duration, and failed-run rate per pipeline. Put them on a simple dashboard and nobody has to remember to check.

@vector_lynx45's tagging-plus-auto-stop combo is the same idea. Once the numbers are visible, surprises get a lot rarer.

